---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@lib/site';

const lastUpdated = 'May 2025';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="Ember & Ink is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program. This page explains our affiliate links and how they support the site."
  url={`${SITE.url}/affiliate-disclosure/`}
>
  <article class="container-ember py-16 md:py-24 max-w-3xl">
    <header>
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted">
        The legal bits
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl md:text-5xl text-burgundy">
        Affiliate Disclosure
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-ember mt-10">
      <h2>Amazon Associates</h2>
      <p>
        Ember &amp; Ink is a participant in the <strong>Amazon Services
        LLC Associates Program</strong>, an affiliate advertising program
        designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by
        advertising and linking to Amazon.com. As an Amazon Associate,
        Ember &amp; Ink earns from qualifying purchases.
      </p>

      <h2>What this means for you</h2>
      <p>
        Some links on this site are <strong>affiliate links</strong> — most
        often "Buy on Amazon" buttons on review pages, or Amazon book
        titles in reading lists. When you click one of these links and
        make a purchase, we may earn a small commission at
        <strong>no additional cost to you</strong>. The price you pay is
        exactly the same as it would be if you had found the book yourself.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we use affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Running a book blog costs money — hosting, domain, cover images,
        and hours of reading and writing. Affiliate commissions help keep
        Ember &amp; Ink free to read and free of intrusive ads. We only
        recommend books we genuinely believe are worth your time.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Affiliate income never influences our reviews.</strong>
        We write honest opinions about books, including critical ones. We
        do not accept payment in exchange for a positive review, and we
        do not remove or soften a review because a book is not monetised
        with affiliate links. If we stop recommending a book, we say so.
      </p>

      <h2>Other affiliate programs</h2>
      <p>
        In the future we may join additional affiliate programs (for
        example, Bookshop.org or an independent bookstore program). Any
        such links will be governed by this same disclosure.
      </p>

      <h2>FTC compliance</h2>
      <p>
        In accordance with the U.S. Federal Trade Commission's
        16 CFR, Part 255 ("Guides Concerning the Use of Endorsements and
        Testimonials"), all affiliate relationships are disclosed here
        and, where relevant, clearly marked in the content itself.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions?</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions about this disclosure, please email
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or use the
        <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>